<!-- ============================================================
     MANIFESTO
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="manifesto" id="manifesto">
  <div class="manifesto-label">Manifesto · the editor's note</div>
  <p>
    <span class="dropcap">T</span>here is a long, half-forgotten tradition of writing limericks about people named Bill. No one can quite say why the name invites trouble — perhaps it is the single syllable, easy to rhyme with hill, sill, spill, and pill. Perhaps it is the way the word sounds, in English, like a small accident about to happen.
  </p>
  <p>
    What follows is a miscellany of twenty-five such Bills, each dispatched in five lines of AABBA. There is a Bill on a hill. There is an economist with a model that will not behave. There is a hermit in a pail. There is even a Bill who keeps company with a man named Jurgen, which is its own kind of trouble.
  </p>
  <p>
    The postcards are arranged in the order they were found. Read them in any order you please. The Bills, in any case, will not behave.
  </p>
</section>

