<section class="limericks" id="limericks">
  <div class="limericks-header">
    <h2>The <span class="em">Postcards</span></h2>
    <div class="meta">
      25 limericks · AABBA · in order<br>
      <span class="sub">filed under: nonsense, mostly</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="limericks-grid">

    <!-- 01 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 01</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">There once was a fellow named Bill,</span>
        <span class="line">Who climbed to the top of a hill.</span>
        <span class="line short">He shouted with glee,</span>
        <span class="line short">"The view I can see!"</span>
        <span class="line">Then tumbled and took a bad spill.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">from the hill, somewhere east</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 02 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 02</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">An economist fellow named Bill,</span>
        <span class="line">Said "markets will move as I will."</span>
        <span class="line short">He plotted a curve,</span>
        <span class="line short">With plenty of nerve,</span>
        <span class="line">And lost all his funds on the spill.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">supply, demand &amp; spill</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 03 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 03</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">Old Bill from the town of Carlisle,</span>
        <span class="line">Would smile in a curious style.</span>
        <span class="line short">He'd grin at the sky,</span>
        <span class="line short">And wave at each fly,</span>
        <span class="line">Then walk down the road for a mile.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">from Carlisle, smiling</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 04 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 04</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">A sailor named Bill from Cape Cod,</span>
        <span class="line">Declared that he'd captured a cod.</span>
        <span class="line short">"It weighed forty stone!"</span>
        <span class="line short">He said with a groan,</span>
        <span class="line">But no one believed him — how odd.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">Cape Cod, forty stone</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 05 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 05</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">Young Bill had a terrible snore,</span>
        <span class="line">That rattled each window and door.</span>
        <span class="line short">His neighbors would flee,</span>
        <span class="line short">To the edge of the sea,</span>
        <span class="line">And sleep on the cold, stony shore.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">the snore, the cold shore</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 06 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 06</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">A baker named Bill from old Rye,</span>
        <span class="line">Would bake bread that reached to the sky.</span>
        <span class="line short">The neighbors, aghast,</span>
        <span class="line short">Cried "bake it less fast!</span>
        <span class="line">Or we'll all be left eating it dry!"</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">Old Rye, raised high</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 07 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 07</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">There was a brave Bill from Kalamazoo,</span>
        <span class="line">Who wrestled a tiger or two.</span>
        <span class="line short">"It's nothing," he said,</span>
        <span class="line short">As they patted his head,</span>
        <span class="line">"Now where is my warm honey-brew?"</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">Kalamazoo, the brave</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 08 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 08</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">A philosopher Bill from Ostend,</span>
        <span class="line">Would think and would think without end.</span>
        <span class="line short">"The meaning of life,"</span>
        <span class="line short">He said to his wife,</span>
        <span class="line">"Is asking what life wants to send."</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">Ostend, still thinking</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 09 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 09</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">There once was a singer named Bill,</span>
        <span class="line">Whose voice carried over the hill.</span>
        <span class="line short">The dogs howled along,</span>
        <span class="line short">Like a chorus of song,</span>
        <span class="line">And neighbors grew quiet and still.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">over the hill, his voice</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 10 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 10</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">A hermit named Bill from the dale,</span>
        <span class="line">Lived inside of a giant red pail.</span>
        <span class="line short">"It keeps out the rain,</span>
        <span class="line short">And the wind, and the pain,"</span>
        <span class="line">He said, looking perfectly pale.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">from the dale, in a pail</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 11 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 11</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">Old Bill had a chicken named Sue,</span>
        <span class="line">Who laid him an egg that was blue.</span>
        <span class="line short">"A miracle!" cried</span>
        <span class="line short">The townsfolk outside,</span>
        <span class="line">"Whatever will roosters now do?"</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">the blue egg, the rooster</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 12 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 12</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">A gambler named Bill from Saint Paul,</span>
        <span class="line">Would bet on whatever would fall.</span>
        <span class="line short">He wagered his cat</span>
        <span class="line short">On a butterfly's spat,</span>
        <span class="line">And now owns no animals at all.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">Saint Paul, lost the cat</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 13 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 13</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">There was a young Bill from old Rome,</span>
        <span class="line">Who never could feel quite at home.</span>
        <span class="line short">He packed up his hat,</span>
        <span class="line short">And sailed on a cat,</span>
        <span class="line">And wandered the world as a gnome.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">Old Rome, the gnome</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 14 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 14</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">A blacksmith named Bill from the hills,</span>
        <span class="line">Made horseshoes and forks and brass grills.</span>
        <span class="line short">His forge burned so bright,</span>
        <span class="line short">It lit up the night,</span>
        <span class="line">And warmed all the village's chills.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">from the hills, the forge</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 15 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 15</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">A poet named Bill from East Troy,</span>
        <span class="line">Found words were his favorite joy.</span>
        <span class="line short">He'd rhyme through the day,</span>
        <span class="line short">In a curious way,</span>
        <span class="line">That puzzled each girl and each boy.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">East Troy, the poet</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 16 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 16</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">There once was a Bill from Quebec,</span>
        <span class="line">Who wore a strange bell on his neck.</span>
        <span class="line short">It rang as he walked,</span>
        <span class="line short">The neighbors all talked,</span>
        <span class="line">And wondered if he was a wreck.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">Quebec, the bell</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 17 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 17</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">A fisherman Bill on the coast,</span>
        <span class="line">Would tell of the fish he'd soon roast.</span>
        <span class="line short">"A whale!" he would cry,</span>
        <span class="line short">With a glint in his eye,</span>
        <span class="line">Then dine on a sliver of toast.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">the coast, the toast</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 18 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 18</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">A doctor named Bill from Dundee,</span>
        <span class="line">Would cure every patient for free.</span>
        <span class="line short">"Your health," he would say,</span>
        <span class="line short">"Is the wealth of the day,"</span>
        <span class="line">And prescribed them a cup of warm tea.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">Dundee, the doctor</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 19 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 19</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">There was an old Bill by a stream,</span>
        <span class="line">Who liked to pretend he could dream.</span>
        <span class="line short">"The fish," he would say,</span>
        <span class="line short">"In their curious way,</span>
        <span class="line">Are plotting some terrible scheme."</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">the stream, the scheme</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 20 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 20</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">A carpenter Bill from Peru,</span>
        <span class="line">Built houses of bamboo and glue.</span>
        <span class="line short">"They'll weather the storm!"</span>
        <span class="line short">He'd say, well-informed,</span>
        <span class="line">Then watched them all blow — only two.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">Peru, only two</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 21 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 21</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">There once was a Bill from Cologne,</span>
        <span class="line">Who lived in a tower of stone.</span>
        <span class="line short">"The view," he declared,</span>
        <span class="line short">"Is to be compared,</span>
        <span class="line">To sitting upon a small throne."</span>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">Cologne, the throne</div>
    </article>

    <!-- 22 -->
    <article class="limerick-card">
      <div class="stamp">posted</div>
      <div class="num">No. 22</div>
      <div class="text">
        <span class="line">A musician named Bill from Bordeaux,</span>
        <span class="line">Played songs that were terribly slow.</span>
        <span class="line short">"It's art," he would say,</span>
        <span class="line short">"In a curious way,</span>
        <span class="line">That nobody happens to know."</span>
      </div>
